# Layer A density v4 fixture: 41-toggle-machine with deeper inference.
#
# v4 vs v2.5:
#   - The `transitionFnT FNT [boolT unitT] resultT` declaration is
#     dropped: it's unreachable from the StateMachine root in the
#     canonical store, so it doesn't affect the hash. Hand-authored
#     Layer A often carries such "decorative" type declarations; the
#     density-v4 form trusts inference and omits them.
#   - The `s:boolT` annotation is elided. The elaborator infers `s`'s
#     paramType from its use as the argument to `APP not [s]` (the
#     `not` builtin's FunctionType is `boolT -> boolT`).
#   - The `e:unitT` annotation is elided. The elaborator infers `e`'s
#     paramType from the StateMachine's transitionFn → (state, event)
#     signature: the second LAM param matches `inputStream`'s eventType
#     (unitT).
#
# Round-trip: canonical hash equals 41-toggle-machine.json's (the
# unreachable transitionFnT node is not part of the reachable graph
# hash, so its omission is hash-neutral).
@v=1 root=toggleMachine
emptyOutputsT PRD []
stateFieldT PRF "state" boolT
outputsFieldT PRF "outputs" emptyOutputsT
resultT PRD [stateFieldT outputsFieldT]
negatedState APP not [s]
emptyOutputsV PV emptyOutputsT []
transitionResult PV resultT [state=negatedState outputs=emptyOutputsV]
transitionLambda LAM [s e] transitionResult
inputStream ESE unitT
toggleMachine SM transitionLambda false [inputStream] [] [receiveFx]
